text:
{
"opening": "This release introduces significant usability improvements to the Arrow API, including a new method for parsing human-readable time strings and greater flexibility in week span calculations. Additionally, we are expanding locale support with several new languages and refining the internal mechanisms for locale registration and validation.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The public API must expose the class `CroatianLocale` for use with Croatian language localization."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The public API must expose the class `LithuanianLocale` for use with Lithuanian language localization."
},
{
"id": "m04",
"text": "The public API must expose the class `LatvianLocale` for use with Latvian language localization."
},
{
"id": "m05",
"text": "The `get_locale` function must correctly identify and return instances of subclasses defined via `__init_subclass__`, ensuring that custom locale classes inherit from `Locale` are properly registered and retrievable by their name."
},
{
"id": "m06",
"text": "The public API must expose the class `LatinLocale` for use with Latin language localization."
},
{
"id": "m08",
"text": "The `Arrow.span` method must accept an optional `week_start` parameter (integer 1-7) to define the starting day of the week, raising a `ValueError` if the value is outside this range, and returning the correct start and end `Arrow` objects for the specified week frame."
},
{
"id": "m09",
"text": "The public API must expose the class `MalayLocale` for use with Malay language localization."
},
{
"id": "m10",
"text": "Locale names should be standardized to use ISO notation with dashes (e.g., 'en-gb') rather than underscores, while maintaining backward compatibility for underscore-based inputs during retrieval."
},
{
"id": "m11",
"text": "The `Arrow.dehumanize` method must accept a human-readable string describing a relative time shift and return a new `Arrow` object adjusted accordingly, supporting various natural language formats and optional locale specifications."
}
]
}
